From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:47:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] Add QuickJS.createSync() and QuickJSInstance.createSync()

create() awaits nothing but WebAssembly.instantiate(), yet a host that
must open a VM inside synchronous code (a paint, a synchronous plugin
API) cannot use it.

createSync() takes the options of create() and instantiates with
new WebAssembly.Instance(). The WASM module, and the modules of the
extensions, should be compiled WebAssembly.Modules; bytes are accepted
and compiled with new WebAssembly.Module(), which browsers refuse on
the main thread for large modules, as the documentation says.

The WASI shim and the memory proxy handed to WASI overrides get the
instance's memory as soon as it is instantiated, before _initialize and
the first VM call into WASI (the runtime reads the clock while it is
created); before that, and after dispose, they throw a clear error
instead of dereferencing null. The memory proxy binds the memory's
methods (grow()) to the memory.

The extension loader is split in two: linkExtension() allocates the
extension's memory and table space and builds its imports, and the
caller instantiates it, asynchronously (loadExtension) or not
(loadExtensionSync).
